# AWS / AI architecture edits — from → to (revised v9 → v10)

Applied 2026-06-10. Reflects: OpenAI models on Azure (all modes) + Anthropic models on AWS (EU-only, SaaS mode only). AWS becomes a second carved-out subservice organisation.

---

## DC 3.1 — Infrastructure (AI compute row)

**FROM**
> | AI compute | Azure OpenAI Service (multiple EU regions — see 3.5) and Azure Document Intelligence (Sweden Central) |

**TO**
> | AI compute | Azure OpenAI Service (OpenAI models; multiple EU regions) and Azure Document Intelligence (Sweden Central) in all modes; plus AWS (Anthropic models, EU regions only) for the SaaS open-platform mode — see 3.4, 3.5, DC 7 |

---

## DC 3.4 — Data (AI processing paragraph)

**FROM**
> Customer content submitted to AI features is processed by Azure OpenAI Service and Azure Document Intelligence within the European Economic Area (Azure regions: Sweden Central, West Europe, France Central, Germany West Central, Norway East). These services are operated by Microsoft as part of the carved-out subservice (see DC 7) and do not use customer data to train third-party models. Audio inputs are transcribed by Azure Speech Service in Sweden Central. No prompts or content are transmitted to OpenAI Inc. or Anthropic PBC directly during the examination period.

**TO**
> Customer content submitted to AI features is processed within the European Economic Area by two hosted-model paths: OpenAI models on Azure OpenAI Service (Azure regions: Sweden Central, West Europe, France Central, Germany West Central, Norway East), used in all modes; and Anthropic models hosted on Amazon Web Services (AWS, EU regions only), used in the SaaS open-platform mode. Document layout/OCR uses Azure Document Intelligence and audio transcription uses Azure Speech Service (Sweden Central). The models run within the Microsoft Azure and AWS subservice environments (see DC 7); customer data is not transmitted to OpenAI Inc. or Anthropic PBC directly, is processed only within the EEA, and is not used to train third-party models.

---

## DC 3.5 — Third-Party Access (subprocessor table)

**FROM** (Azure row)
> | Microsoft Azure | Primary cloud infrastructure (sole carved-out subservice organisation). Includes Azure OpenAI Service (LLM + embeddings), Azure Document Intelligence (OCR + layout), Azure Speech Service (audio transcription), and Azure Communication Services (transactional email send). |

**TO** (Azure row reworded + new AWS row)
> | Microsoft Azure | Primary cloud infrastructure (carved-out subservice organisation). Includes Azure OpenAI Service (OpenAI LLM + embeddings), Azure Document Intelligence (OCR + layout), Azure Speech Service (audio transcription), and Azure Communication Services (transactional email send). |
> | Amazon Web Services (AWS) | Hosts Anthropic models for AI features in the SaaS open-platform mode (EU regions only); carved-out subservice organisation for that path. Not used in dedicated-tenant / enterprise deployments. |

---

## DC 3.5 — Third-Party Access (trailing paragraph)

**FROM**
> OpenAI and Anthropic are not part of the production data path during the examination period; they are used only in non-production (development) environments and do not process customer production data. Anthropic is nonetheless maintained as a disclosed subprocessor in the DPA (Appendix B, Table 2), consistent with Normain's practice of keeping approved subprocessors listed to avoid frequent list changes. Application error tracking via Sentry is not currently deployed. Activation of any additional production subprocessor is notified to customers under the DPA's 14-day subprocessor-change notice (DC 2).

**TO**
> OpenAI and Anthropic are the providers of the AI models used in production; their models are hosted within the Azure (OpenAI, all modes) and AWS (Anthropic, SaaS mode only) subservice environments rather than called via the providers' own endpoints, so customer data is not transmitted to OpenAI Inc. or Anthropic PBC directly. Both are disclosed subprocessors in the DPA (Appendix B). Application error tracking via Sentry is not currently deployed. Activation of any additional production subprocessor is notified to customers under the DPA's 14-day subprocessor-change notice (DC 2).

---

## DC 7 — CSOCs (intro)

**FROM**
> The system uses Microsoft Azure as the sole carved-out subservice organization for the production data path. Other named third parties listed in DC 3.5 either receive non-database telemetry (BetterStack), product-analytics events (PostHog), or per-request fetches against customer-supplied URLs (Firecrawl) and are not relied on for the trust services criteria below.
>
> Azure OpenAI Service, Azure Document Intelligence, Azure Speech Service, and Azure Communication Services are operated by Microsoft as part of the Azure subservice and are covered by the same Microsoft Azure SOC 2 Type 2 report.

**TO**
> The system uses two carved-out subservice organizations for the production data path: Microsoft Azure (all modes) and Amazon Web Services (AWS), which hosts Anthropic models in the SaaS open-platform mode. Other named third parties listed in DC 3.5 receive non-database telemetry (BetterStack) or product-analytics events (PostHog) and are not relied on for the trust services criteria below.
>
> Azure OpenAI Service, Azure Document Intelligence, Azure Speech Service, and Azure Communication Services are operated by Microsoft as part of the Azure subservice and are covered by the Microsoft Azure SOC 2 Type 2 report. The Anthropic models used in SaaS mode are hosted on AWS and covered by the AWS SOC 2 Type 2 report.

