## DC 9 — Significant Changes

**FROM**
> No significant changes to the system have been identified during the audit period as of the draft cut-off date (2026-05-18). This section will be re-verified prior to issuance against (a) merges to the default branch of the product repository on or after 2026-05-04, (b) the Linear "Change" issue type for the same window, and (c) published release notes.
>
> No new subprocessors were introduced during the examination period. The subprocessor list of record (DPA Appendix B) was last updated 25 February 2026, before the period start. To be re-confirmed at issuance against the Linear "Subprocessor Change" issue type and Vanta vendor inventory.

**TO**
> During the audit period, Anthropic large-language-model inference was introduced into the SaaS open-platform mode, hosted on AWS (EU regions only) as a new carved-out subservice organisation [effective date to confirm at issuance]. The change followed the change-management and vendor-onboarding process: AWS vendor due diligence and its SOC 2 report were recorded in Vanta, and the subprocessor addition was notified to customers under the DPA with implementation deferred more than 30 days after notice. The DPA subprocessor list (Appendix B) was updated accordingly.
>
> No other significant changes have been identified as of the draft cut-off date. This section will be re-verified prior to issuance against (a) merges to the default branch on or after 2026-05-04, (b) the Linear "Change" issue type, (c) published release notes, and (d) the Vanta vendor inventory and "Subprocessor Change" records.

